{
  "id": "V22",
  "title": "Robustness — awkward inputs",
  "intent": "Valid but awkward inputs: numbers typed with spaces or left blank, a level with lateral load but no wall, walls touching both line ends, zero gravity (blank wall weight and a blank uniform load), a wall with h/b > 3.5 and a manual nailing lighter than needed. The item must calculate and render every tab; the problems must be reported: G2 fails at the level without a wall, the h/b > 3.5 wall is flagged and carries no shear, and the under-nailed wall shows D/C > 1.",
  "covers": [
    "Input parsing (blank / whitespace)",
    "G2 horizontal equilibrium",
    "SDPWS 2021 §4.3.4 h/b > 3.5",
    "Manual nailing NG",
    "Rendering with no gravity"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Parsing: S_DS \" 1.0 \" → 1.0 (so the ASD uplift factor 0.6 − 0.14 × 1.0 = 0.46), ρ \" \" → 1.0, Level 1 floor-to-floor \"10\" → 10 ft, wind \"  \" / \"\" → 0, wall weight psf \"\" → 0, uniform D \" \" → 0: no gravity anywhere."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Level 2 has 1.0E = 2 k but no wall in this line → G2 (horizontal equilibrium) fails at Level 2 (expected 2 k, carried 0). The load still accumulates into the Level 1 story shear: V = 2 + 4 = 6 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "SW-2 (x = 17.5–20.0 ft, touching the line end): h/b = 10/2.5 = 4.0 > 3.5 → not a shear wall (SDPWS 2021 §4.3.4), carries no shear, audit warning. SW-1 (x = 0–8, touching the line start) takes all 6 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-1 manual 6\" o.c.: v = 0.7 × 6000/8 = 525.00 plf vs 312 plf → D/C = 1.683 > 1 → wall NG (a design result, not an equilibrium check)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "SW-1 end forces (no gravity): N = 6 × 10/8 = 7.50 k → T = C = 0.7 × 7.50 = 5.25 k → HDUE5 (5,375 lb; HDUE3 3,790 lb too small), posts (3)2x4 (the (2)2x4 minimum post has 5.00 k < 5.25 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "SW-1 δ at 1.0E: v = 750 plf, A = 15.75 in², G_a = 16 → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0280, vh/(1000G_a) = 0.4688, Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD of HDUE5 = 0.205 × 7500 / 7525 = 0.2043, r = 0.7619 (0.73–1.0) → Δ_c = 0.02 × (1 + (r − 0.73)/0.27) = 0.0224, h·Δa/b = 0.2834 → δ = 0.7801 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Seismic inputs typed with spaces: C_d \" 4 \" → 4, I_e \"1.0 \" → 1.0, risk category II (Ω₀ blank → default 2.5). SW-2 (h/b > 3.5) has no share and no δ; Level 2 has no wall, so no drift row. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.7801 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.7801 / 1.0 = 3.120 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → NG — over the limit (design pinned, so drift sizing does not change it; the line reports drift NG)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Every other line check passes; every tab, calc sheet, elevation and PDF section renders (runner T4)."
    }
  ],
  "expect": [
